# =============================================================================
# Recommended .gitignore for the VAULT CONTENT repo (not for this repo).
# =============================================================================
# Copy this to the root of the vault repo as `.gitignore`. Without it, the
# bridge's `git add -A` bakes per-device UI churn and Obsidian Sync's own
# conflict copies permanently into vault history.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignoring `.obsidian/` wholesale: the plugin/theme declaration
# there is real, low-churn configuration worth versioning, and agents are meant
# to be able to change it.
# =============================================================================

# Per-device UI state - rewrites on nearly every interaction, carries no content.
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/workspace.json.bak

# Obsidian's soft-delete holding pen, not vault content.
.trash/

# Plugin caches and local indices - regenerate on open, large and binary-ish.
.obsidian/cache/
.obsidian/plugins/**/cache/
.obsidian/plugins/**/*.cache
.obsidian/plugins/*/data.json.bak

# NOTE: conflicted-copy notes are deliberately NOT ignored. They are the
# surfacing mechanism: a genuine same-region collision is committed as
# "Note (conflicted copy <timestamp>).md" so it appears on every device,
# inside Obsidian, where Sync's own conflicts appear. Ignoring them would
# hide conflicts in a server log nobody reads.

# obsidian-headless state must live outside the vault tree (it holds the auth
# token). This is a guard against it ever landing here by mistake.
.obsidian-headless/

# OS cruft that ends up inside vault directories.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
